1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:44,000
His arms now restored by the Queen of Witches, Asta and the others were fighting to protect the forest from enemy forces when they were suddenly confronted by Fauna, a leading member of the Eye of the Midnight Sun who also possesses a third eye.

5
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
She's got a third eye too!

6
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Everything is riding on this single shot!

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Water creation magic! Sea dragons roar!

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Our heroes appeared to be helpless as Fauna's fire spirit, Salamander, began to lay waste to the forest.

9
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
But thanks to a powerful attack generated by Noelle's water magic, they were able to subdue the terrible beast.

10
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Okay! Finally time for my special move!

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
For the finishing blow, Asta used Bulthrust, a fighting technique he had just invented.

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Here we go!

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Bulthrust!

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Bulthrust!

15
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Manicom

16
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
This piece began revealing

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:19,980
Thank you.

18
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:49,980
Thank you.

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Thank you.

20
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,620
So it appears he wasn't all bark and no bite.

21
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:25,960
And those other troops.

22
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:39,060
I don't know who this is, but I'm guessing he isn't a witch.

23
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,860
He must have guts to stand up to this huge army all by himself.

24
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,060
Either that or he's stupid.

25
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,800
Mars, you remember me, right?

26
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:50,500
Wait a minute now.

27
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,460
I might be totally off base here.

28
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,800
I think that guy's our old teacher.

29
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:56,940
Yes, Landros.

30
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,940
And it looks like I get the honor of tormenting you.

31
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:02,800
Lucky me.

32
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,260
Me!

33
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:11,040
Ooh, still got it, huh?

34
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,640
You two have changed quite a bit.

35
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,620
And I can see that it's not for the better.

36
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,340
You leave me no choice.

37
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:23,840
But to atone for my mistake.

38
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:26,640
Ooh, feel that breeze?

39
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:27,940
Nice and gentle.

40
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,380
I'll ask you this one time.

41
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:32,900
Any chance you'll turn back?

42
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,020
Ha ha ha!

43
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:38,440
Well, we're the ones with the army, so I'm thinking that's our line.

44
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,180
See, here's the thing.

45
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:43,720
It turns out our king isn't in the best of health these days.

46
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:45,540
And from what we've been hearing,

47
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:49,860
the Queen of Witches has been around for hundreds of years now.

48
00:04:50,340 --> 00:04:52,440
The king wants to find out her secret,

49
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:55,620
even if it means wiping out everyone in this pitiful forest.

50
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:58,920
So when we got word that the Eye of the Midnight Sun

51
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,120
was already planning to stir up trouble here,

52
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:04,000
we thought we might as well take advantage of the confusion

53
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,600
and make this a real party.

54
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:08,160
We want something.

55
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,720
We take it by force.

56
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:12,980
That's always been our philosophy in the Diamond Kingdom, right?

57
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:15,540
Which is why I left and never went back.

58
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:19,900
Now!

59
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:21,260
Woo-hoo-hoo!

60
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:24,200
Sure is good to see you again, Teach!

61
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:26,520
Ha!

62
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:33,300
All these soldiers finished charging right for us!

63
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:34,420
Is he crazy?

64
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:36,700
When creation...

65
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:40,340
Emperor of Slashing Winds, Winter wins!

66
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,140
Here it comes!

67
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:44,480
He's fast!

68
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:48,540
Wait!

69
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:49,520
I know him!

70
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:52,560
It's that traitorous coward, Fonzel Kruger.

71
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:54,640
He was a Diamond Kingdom commander

72
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,600
and combat instructor before he double-crossed us.

73
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:00,860
And he's got a sizable bounty on his head as well.

74
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,620
Let's take him down now!

75
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:15,360
They're not moving.

76
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:18,980
Must be hard to attack when your allies are that close together.

77
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:23,640
Especially with the powerful magic ability that those two resist.

78
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:28,220
But there's only so much one man can do.

79
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:31,680
I'll have to depend on my other half and my student.

80
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:40,760
I wonder if my master ever put clothes on.

81
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:40,840
I wonder if my master ever put clothes on.

82
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:48,560
There.

83
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:50,500
I am such a genius!

84
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,460
Remain calm!

85
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:55,500
Assume formation number six!

86
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,520
Even if he is a former commander,

87
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:59,880
if you follow orders and strike from afar,

88
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,200
then he will fall!

89
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,660
He is your only target!

90
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:07,780
That's not exactly accurate.

91
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:11,100
No matter how many troops your opponent has,

92
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,420
you should always attack with three times as many.

93
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:15,140
That's what master told me.

94
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,080
It's an ambush!

95
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,340
We'll be fine.

96
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:18,660
We have plenty of soldiers.

97
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:19,320
Go!

98
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:20,080
Squad two!

99
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:29,300
What?

100
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,220
They're pushing us into the forest.

101
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,240
There's no way this will work with all these trees and fog.

102
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:42,020
Let's switch to formation 13!

103
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:43,360
Squad four!

104
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:46,360
Squad five!

105
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:51,240
How are they able to predict our every move?

106
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:52,440
Easy.

107
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:53,780
Not so long ago,

108
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,320
I was on the Diamond Kingdom's assassination squad.

109
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:58,860
You aren't even a challenge.

110
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:12,820
I used to kill people

111
00:08:12,820 --> 00:08:14,780
who were just doing their best to survive.

112
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:17,600
Simply so that I could stay alive myself.

113
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:36,360
Maybe I'm hoping to make up for what I've done.

114
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:39,720
Or maybe I'm just patting myself on the back.

115
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:47,600
But still, I'm going to stop you.

116
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:52,100
You're a damn traitor.

117
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:53,200
True.

118
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:56,580
But there's nothing you can say that'll make me change my mind now.

119
00:08:56,580 --> 00:09:00,060
If I back down,

120
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:03,800
then the person who saved my life won't be very happy with me.

121
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,180
That girl's a fierce one,

122
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:10,240
jumping right in there and taking command of so many people.

123
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:11,520
Oh, I agree.

124
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:13,620
Our Mariela sure is something.

125
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,560
Now for the next phase.

126
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:19,060
What's happening?

127
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:29,880
And there you have it.

128
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:32,840
Thanks to my superior magic items and tinkering skills,

129
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:35,620
I was able to give those security golems a little upgrade.

130
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,040
That's marvelous.

131
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:40,000
I'm sure it must have been expensive to pull off them.

132
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:40,900
You won't believe this,

133
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:43,880
but the materials only cost me about 3,000 yule each.

134
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:45,820
That much destruction for so cheap?

135
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:46,520
What a value.

136
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,580
Now's our chance, ladies.

137
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:52,140
Don't let those lawless brutes ransack our beautiful forest.

138
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:54,680
Show them that these witches mean business.

139
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,160
Whoa, whoa.

140
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:01,860
They set a trap down there thinking we would barrel right into it.

141
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:05,280
It's probably better if we tread carefully,

142
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,260
but it kind of looks like fun,

143
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,600
so here I go.

144
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,840
Whatever the game is, let's play.

145
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:16,240
Now then, where could they be?

146
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:17,660
Uh-oh.

147
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,740
Exactly what I thought you'd do.

148
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,420
That's enough, Ladros.

149
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:22,500
Windbinding magic.

150
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:24,060
Emperor of slashing winds.

151
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:24,740
Whirlwind.

152
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,040
Aw, rats.

153
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:28,740
Guess you got me.

154
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:30,980
For the last time,

155
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,840
do you want to turn around?

156
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:33,860
Hmm.

157
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:38,260
Now where would be the fun in that?

158
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:41,260
I've got so much more slaughtering left to do.

159
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,760
What's wrong with you?

160
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:43,300
Huh?

161
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:46,760
You can't train us to be killing machines

162
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:50,160
only to expect us to behave like upstanding citizens

163
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:52,380
and during a big battle like this?

164
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,260
I'm sorry,

165
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:54,920
but I promised.

166
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:59,080
See, I told my last pupil,

167
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,300
someone younger than you.

168
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:03,760
I'm done running.

169
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,380
I'm gonna live.

170
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:26,220
That's it.

171
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,720
Feel your opponent's mana.

172
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:28,320
Hmm.

173
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:30,400
Hmm?

174
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,280
Calm your emotions.

175
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:34,740
Good job.

176
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:35,660
Try to focus.

177
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,200
Listen.

178
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:40,100
Your powers are meant for protecting people

179
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:41,140
and nothing else.

180
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,500
Don't ever forget that, okay?

181
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:44,820
Right!

182
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:58,100
His strength was physical reinforcement spells.

183
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:00,520
I'll never win like this.

184
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,520
Don't move or you're dead.

185
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:09,680
Mars.

186
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,960
Of all the students I taught,

187
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,000
he was the most skilled.

188
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,720
There's no way I stand a chance against him at this distance.

189
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,320
I'll have to make some room.

190
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,580
Wind creation magic.

191
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,320
Emperor of slashing winds.

192
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:25,040
Mountain wind!

193
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,720
Wind creation magic.

194
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:39,680
I'm putting my all into this.

195
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:42,720
Now, wind creation magic.

196
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:44,640
Emperor of slashing winds.

197
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:56,780
Not having an elemental attribute always made him feel a little odd.

198
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:58,780
Sir?

199
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,500
I don't need an attribute to be strong, right?

200
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:07,140
He gave himself a complex over it.

201
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:12,060
But he still had greater power than any of his peers.

202
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,220
If he knows a long-range spell, I'm done for.

203
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,380
I'd better put him out quick.

204
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,800
Forgive me.

205
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:21,620
No!

206
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:24,200
Stop it!

207
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:25,120
I can't!

208
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:25,500
I can't!

209
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:25,880
I can't!

210
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:26,260
I can't!

211
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:27,020
I can't!

212
00:13:27,020 --> 00:13:28,940
No more of your magic, sir!

213
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:29,360
Please!

214
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:32,200
I'm downright stuffed.

215
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:36,540
Are you surprised?

216
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,660
There's not a scratch on him.

217
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,120
Yeah, I've made a few changes.

218
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:48,300
After you left, the army gave me one of those upgrade surgeries, and I came out with some new tricks.

219
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:50,480
Absorption and a mission.

220
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:58,160
My body could suck up any magic attack that's thrown at it, and I can release that gathered force whenever I like.

221
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:00,200
You know what that means, right?

222
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:05,560
Not only am I about to kill all your little buddies, I'm gonna use your magic to do it!

223
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:07,080
What's this power from?

224
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:09,020
It's not just Ladros.

225
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:11,200
There's so much, it must be something else.

226
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:16,780
By the way, Teach, you didn't happen to bring any loved ones into the forest, did you?

227
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:20,800
Because if you did, you might want to go check on them real quick.

228
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:27,820
And you'll have to outrun my magic, so you'd better hurry up!

229
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:32,660
On your marks, get set, go!

230
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:36,140
Million lasers!

231
00:14:41,200 --> 00:15:03,440
Oh, whoopsie!

232
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:06,840
I got so excited there that I wiped out my own guys!

233
00:15:07,180 --> 00:15:08,800
I wonder if Teach made it!

234
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:11,600
Ah, there you are!

235
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:15,640
Sal!

236
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:16,720
Oh no!

237
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:17,740
Domino!

238
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,700
Look at that!

239
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:24,340
So you did have someone special here, after all.

240
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:27,740
But why haven't you introduced us?

241
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:29,700
Don't you have any manners?

242
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:31,360
Wow!

243
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:34,680
You didn't tell me your lady friend was such a looker!

244
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,000
I'm jealous!

245
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:40,900
Hey, wait!

246
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:42,620
Haven't I seen you before?

247
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:43,920
Oh yeah!

248
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:44,900
That's right!

249
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:48,000
You're the little minx he decided to run away with, aren't you?

250
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,620
So, how have you been?

251
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,220
Ladros, stop!

252
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,520
Please, I beg you.

253
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:54,240
Use your power for what's right!

254
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:54,800
Of course!

255
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,580
I am, and I always have!

256
00:15:56,580 --> 00:16:01,840
Come on, you and I both know that combat training was never meant to teach us how to protect anybody!

257
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:09,400
There's nothing better than using your power to the absolute max and devastating any opponent that dares stand in your way!

258
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:13,480
My goal is to be recognized all over this nation, and eventually the whole world!

259
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:17,280
That's why I trained hard and rose through the ranks to become one of the eight shining generals!

260
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:22,060
Why are you always spewing this idealistic garbage?

261
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:27,660
No wonder you were defeated in that power struggle and had to flee the Diamond Kingdom with your tail between your legs!

262
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:29,260
You're such a coward!

263
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,560
Shut your mouth right now!

264
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:35,360
My cell is no coward!

265
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:39,000
I think I'll start by killing this noisy little witch!

266
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:39,640
I think I'll try to kill you!

267
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:52,540
Domino!

268
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:05,680
My powers are for protecting people.

269
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:14,680
people. Everything that you said, well, I guess it finally hit home. Mars, I...

270
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:22,360
